Krita Nova 24 - the Brush Panel ignores palm rejection (Android)

Palm rejection (patch 09) only filters touches on the canvas. On Android a
touch sequence goes to the window under its first finger, though, so with a
palm resting on the canvas a finger on the Brush Panel arrived at the canvas
as part of the palm's sequence and was ignored along with it.

PanelTouchRouter (KisMainWindow.cpp, Android only) watches touch sequences
arriving at other windows. A finger that goes down over the floating Brush
Panel, its "more" popup or a popup opened from it is forwarded to the widget
under it as mouse press / move / release, so buttons, the size and opacity
sliders, the colours and the grip work while the palm rests on the canvas or
the pen is in use. A sequence that starts on the panel reaches it as before.
